<div class="container">
  <h1 class="text-xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 2026/09/26</p>
  <p class="pt-4">
    YouCongress ("us", "we", or "our") operates https://youcongress.org (the "Site"). This page informs you of our policies regarding the collection, use and disclosure of Personal Information we receive from users of the Site.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use your Personal Information only for providing and improving the Site. By using the Site, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-6"><b>Cookies and Analytics</b></p>
  <p>
    We use essential cookies to operate the Site, including cookies for security, sign-in,
    session continuity, and remembering your cookie preference.
  </p>
  <p>
    With your permission, we use Amplitude to understand how signed-in users interact with the
    Site so we can improve it. We do not send usage events to Amplitude unless you select
    “Accept” in the cookie banner. You can accept, reject, or change this choice at any time by
    selecting “Cookie settings” in the footer. Your choice is stored for up to one year.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-4"><b>Information Collection And Use</b></p>
  <p>
    While using our Site, we may ask you to provide us with certain personally identifiable information that can be used to contact or identify you. Personally identifiable information may include, but is not limited to your name ("Personal Information").
  </p>
  <p class="pt-4"><b>Log Data</b></p>
  <p>
    Like many site operators, we collect information that your browser sends whenever you visit our Site ("Log Data").
  </p>
  <p>
    This Log Data may include information such as your computer's Internet Protocol ("IP") address, browser type, browser version, the pages of our Site that you visit, the time and date of your visit, the time spent on those pages and other statistics.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you consent to analytics, Amplitude may process usage event data on our behalf. We also
    use Plausible for aggregate, cookie-free traffic analytics.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-4"><b>Communications</b></p>
  <p>
    If you subscribe, we use your email address to send YouCongress newsletters. These may
    include sourced quotes and news about AI governance, AI safety, and the impact of AI on jobs,
    as well as occasional YouCongress product updates. You can unsubscribe at any time using the
    link included in every newsletter.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use Substack Inc. to manage newsletter subscriptions and deliver newsletters. Substack
    processes subscriber information, such as email addresses and newsletter engagement data, to
    provide these services. Substack's handling of Personal Information is also described in its <a
      href="https://substack.com/privacy"
      class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800"
    >
      Privacy Policy
    </a>.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-4"><b>International Data Transfers</b></p>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers, including Substack, may process Personal Information in the
    United States or other countries outside your country of residence. Where required, we rely on
    appropriate contractual safeguards, including standard contractual clauses, for these
    transfers.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-4"><b>Security</b></p>
  <p>
    The security of your Personal Information is important to us, but remember that no method of transmission over the Internet, or method of electronic storage, is 100% secure. While we strive to use commercially acceptable means to protect your Personal Information, we cannot guarantee its absolute security.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-4"><b>Changes To This Privacy Policy</b></p>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy is effective as of 2026/09/26 and will remain in effect except with respect to any changes in its provisions in the future, which will be in effect immediately after being posted on this page.
  </p>
  <p>
    We reserve the right to update or change our Privacy Policy at any time and you should check this Privacy Policy periodically. Your continued use of the Service after we post any modifications to the Privacy Policy on this page will constitute your acknowledgment of the modifications and your consent to abide and be bound by the modified Privacy Policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we make any material changes to this Privacy Policy, we will notify you either through the email address you have provided us, or by placing a prominent notice on our website.
  </p>

  <p class="pt-4"><b>Contact Us</b></p>
  <p>
    If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us: support@youcongress.org
  </p>
</div>
